    {
      "key": "oteryn:quest-npc/tibia_tales/corym_servant/greet-other",
      "quest": "oteryn:quest.tibia_tales",
      "npc": "oteryn:npc.corym_servant",
      "trigger": "greet",
      "keywords": [],
      "guards": [],
      "reply": [
        "Every man is the architect of his own fortune. The times of repression are finally over."
      ],
      "effects": [],
      "sources": [
        "canary:04b83b512114bfd888000d6e1433ed8ecaec7c5b:data-otservbr-global/npc/corym_servant.lua:78"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "oteryn:quest-npc/tibia_tales/corym_servant/resources",
      "quest": "oteryn:quest.tibia_tales",
      "npc": "oteryn:npc.corym_servant",
      "trigger": "say",
      "keywords": [
        "decreasing resources"
      ],
      "guards": [],
      "reply": [
        "You have to know, that our work is very hard and the conditions we have are terrible. The wanted amount is abolutely unrealistic. Beyond that the food we get is never enough. ...",
        "Our workers should give their best while starving. This is not possible. That's the point to {defy} the authority."
      ],
      "effects": [
        {
          "kind": "set_topic",
          "value": 1
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        "canary:04b83b512114bfd888000d6e1433ed8ecaec7c5b:data-otservbr-global/npc/corym_servant.lua:91"
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "oteryn:quest-npc/tibia_tales/corym_servant/defy",
      "quest": "oteryn:quest.tibia_tales",
      "npc": "oteryn:npc.corym_servant",
      "trigger": "say",
      "keywords": [
        "defy"
      ],
      "guards": [
        {
          "kind": "storage",
          "track": "oteryn:quest-progress/quest/u11_50/hidden_threats/quest_line",
          "op": "eq",
          "value": 1
        }
      ],
      "reply": [
        "I see you are interested to change our sitation. The first thing I like you to do is to liberate the jailed coryms. There are three areas with locked doors. You have to find a way to get access. ...",
        "For this reason I will give you access to the second floor. It was closed because it wasn't possible to continue working at these enourmous high temperatures. Furthermore we were instantly attacked by stonerefiners. So take care of you!"
      ],
